 In this problem, we are asked to find out how many dozens of Claire eats in 4 weeks.
To solve this, we need to convert the number of eggs Claire eats per morning and the duration of time into a common unit, which is eggs for the number of eggs and weeks for the duration.

Since there are 12 eggs in a dozen, we first calculate the number of eggs Claire eats in a week:

\begin{aligned}
\text{Eggs per week} & = \text{Eggs per morning} \times \text{Days per week} \\
& = 3 \times 7 \\
& = 21\,\text{eggs}
\end{aligned}

Now, we need to determine the number of dozen eggs Claire eats in a week:

\begin{aligned}
\text{Dozens per week} & = \frac{\text{Eggs per week}}{12} \\
& = \frac{21}{12} \approx 1.75\,\text{dozens}
\end{aligned}

Since we cannot have a fraction of a dozen eggs, we round the value up. So Claire eats approximately \boxed{2} dozens of eggs in a week.

Finally, we calculate the number of dozens of eggs Claire eats in 4 weeks:

\begin{aligned}
\text{Dozens in 4 weeks} & = \text{Dozen per week} \times 4 \\
& = 2\, \text{dozens} \times 4 \\
& = \boxed{8} \,\text{dozen eggs}
\end{aligned}

So, Claire eats approximately 8 dozen eggs in 4 weeks.

